course: dictionary
lesson: 9170
title: Reading abbreviations
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or name, often made from the first letters. SNP is an abbreviation. You cannot always tell its meaning from the letters alone, so look at the words around it. Context is the clue.
explain: «The SNP, the Scottish National Party, wants Scotland to become independent from the UK.» The words after the comma explain the letters: S is for Scottish, N is for National, P is for Party. Independent means running itself, not being part of another country.
explain: The same letters can mean something different in another subject. «SNP» said «snip» is a science word, a single-nucleotide polymorphism. Ask yourself what the topic is: politics or biology? The topic tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or name, often using its first letters.
fact: SNP stands for the Scottish National Party, a political party in Scotland.
fact: The SNP wants Scotland to become an independent country, separate from the United Kingdom.
fact: In science, an SNP (said «snip») is a single-nucleotide polymorphism: one letter of DNA that differs between people.
fact: Phrases like «SNP leader», «SNP MPs» and «vote SNP» show the political meaning.
exercise: «The SNP, the Scottish National Party, wants Scotland to become independent.» What does SNP stand for here? | *Scottish National Party | Scotland National Problem | Single-nucleotide polymorphism | Small New Plan
exercise: An SNP, said «snip», is a science word. Which subject is it from? | Cooking | *Biology, about DNA | Music lessons | Football
exercise: «Smaller parties bring their own big topics, like the Greens with the environment or the SNP with Scotland running itself.» What is the SNP in this sentence? | A Scottish football club | A single letter of DNA | *A political party | A type of DNA change
test: Why is SNP called an abbreviation? | *It is a short form made from the first letters of longer words | It is a long sentence about Scotland | It is a kind of weather | It is a number used in maths
test: In science, what does a single-nucleotide polymorphism show? | A type of party game | A kind of Scottish castle | *A place where one letter of DNA differs between people | A vote in Parliament
exam: What does the SNP want for Scotland? | To stop all voting in Scotland | To change its name to the United Kingdom | To have no parliament at all | *To become an independent country, separate from the UK
